@page "/"
@layout Layout.PublicLayout

<PageTitle>EngineOS — Your Engineering Partner</PageTitle>

<div class="welcome-hero">
    <h1 class="welcome-title">EngineOS</h1>
    <p class="welcome-subtitle">Your engineering partner.</p>
    <p class="welcome-description">
        Understand the work. Keep the context. Coordinate the workers.
    </p>

    <div class="welcome-explanation">
        <p>
            EngineOS maintains durable engineering context across sessions.
            It knows what your project is, what has been accomplished, what remains,
            and what should happen next — without depending on conversation history.
        </p>
        <p>
            Coding agents like GitHub Copilot and Kiro perform the implementation.
            EngineOS prepares the right context, hands off to the right worker,
            evaluates the result, and keeps the engineering state current.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="welcome-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/app?start=build">Start Building</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline btn-lg" href="/repository">Work with Existing Software</a>
    </div>

    <div class="welcome-detail">
        <div class="welcome-card">
            <h3>Start Building</h3>
            <p>Begin with an idea. Describe your project in conversation and EngineOS will establish the engineering context, track decisions, and coordinate work.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="welcome-card">
            <h3>Work with Existing Software</h3>
            <p>Point EngineOS at an existing repository. It discovers the engineering structure, builds an understanding, and becomes your ongoing engineering partner.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    // Root welcome page. Entry point for EngineOS.
    // Two paths: conversation-first (Start Building) or repository-first (Existing Software).
}
